            {
              "id": "a6cfabca-f3ca-3ce8-8270-e6f1abbdd75f",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible undefined behavior risk due to overlapping memory regions between the source and destination buffers in the call to the string copy function. The risk is confirmed by dataflow analysis, which indicates that the source and destination may refer to overlapping memory. Additionally, the source may be null at this call site, which further increases the risk of undefined behavior. There is no explicit null-termination of the destination buffer after the copy, and no evidence that the length argument is derived from the destination's capacity. The destination is guarded as non-null, but this does not mitigate the overlap or null source risks. The classification and verdict both indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the undefined behavior risk caused by possible overlapping memory regions in the string copy operation, first ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap. If overlap is possible, use a memory-safe function such as `memmove` instead of `strncpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Additionally, always ensure that the destination buffer is properly null-terminated after the copy to prevent string-related vulnerabilities.\n\n**Example fix:**\n\n```cpp\n// Ensure source and destination do not overlap, or use memmove if overlap is possible\nmemmove(info->name, reinterpret_cast<char *>(vbios.name), AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\n// Explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer\ninfo->name[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
