            {
              "id": "17a0f40a-2e6f-3df8-89a9-ef7793a9a277",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies data from a C-style string into a character buffer using a length argument of 'len-1', but there is no check to ensure that 'len' is greater than zero. If 'len' is zero or negative, subtracting one can result in a very large value due to unsigned integer underflow, potentially causing a buffer overflow or other memory corruption. The source is a C-style string, which is generally safe, and there is no risk of overlapping memory regions or null pointers at this call site. However, the absence of a guard to ensure the length is positive is a critical issue. The destination buffer is a pointer, and there is no evidence that the length is derived from the buffer's actual capacity, increasing the risk. There is also no explicit null-termination after the copy, which can lead to further issues. The classification and verdict both indicate a high likelihood of a real vulnerability.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying data into the destination buffer, ensure that the length argument is greater than zero to prevent unsigned integer underflow. Add a check to verify that 'len' is greater than zero before performing the copy. Also, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer after copying to avoid unterminated strings.\n\n```cpp\nif (len > 0) {\n    std::strncpy(version, empty.c_str(), len - 1);\n    version[len - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\nThis approach prevents the underflow and ensures the buffer is properly null-terminated.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
